id: ops-jzp5
title: Hoisted broken pm-ops can bypass merge-driver install guard
description: "Greptile found that the canonical prepare launcher searches only the consumer checkout node_modules/pm-ops after a MODULE_NOT_FOUND resolution. Node also resolves packages from ancestor node_modules. If a hoisted pm-ops directory exists but lacks package.json, the launcher treats it as an omit-dev install and silently skips field-aware merge-driver registration. This extends the local broken-install guard in ops-eyi8 to the full Node lookup path."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-26T16:43:46.361Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-26T16:57:51.563Z"
assignee: codex
claim_principal: codex
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "A real child checkout with an empty ancestor node_modules/pm-ops fails the prepare hook without the omit-dev skip notice; a truly absent package still skips once; an intact hoisted pm-ops runs the installer; the regression fails on the old template, full release:check and strict PM health pass; consumer copies update only after a canonical pm-ops release."
